{"id":"effect-f1166714-7ec7-53a8-b602-79404ff97ae1","sessionId":"cb1b579b-a4ed-295c-9696-f1030ea14b38","turnId":"turn-8bd04679712c34ce8e7fb14ef01d9362","inputEntryId":"user-turn-8bd04679712c34ce8e7fb14ef01d9362-1","createdAt":1794279806278,"updatedAt":1794279806301,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.read_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.read_file","display":{"summary":"Reading src/app.py","content":null,"suffix":"","verb":"Reading","message":"src/app.py","settledVerb":"Read","settledMessage":"src/app.py","statusText":"Reading file"},"kind":"file_read","input":{"filePath":"src/app.py","offset":null,"limit":2000}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-MZ7H8q/src/app.py","content":"\"\"\"Story library: the publish handler.\n\nEach story is stored in one DynamoDB item together with the three most similar\nstories already in the library (``similar``), so the reader page can show\n\"related\" without a query at read time.\n\"\"\"\nimport json\nimport logging\nimport re\nimport time\nfrom decimal import Decimal\n\nlog = logging.getLogger(\"stories\")\n\nTABLE_NAME = \"stories\"\nTOP_N = 3\n\n_WORD = re.compile(r\"[a-z0-9]+\")\n\n\ndef words(text):\n    return set(_WORD.findall((text or \"\").lower()))\n\n\ndef similarity(a, b):\n    \"\"\"Shared-tag ratio (Jaccard), blended with shared words of the two bodies.\"\"\"\n    ta, tb = set(a.get(\"tags\", [])), set(b.get(\"tags\", []))\n    tag_score = len(ta & tb) / len(ta | tb) if (ta | tb) else 0\n    wa, wb = words(a.get(\"body\")), words(b.get(\"body\"))\n    word_score = len(wa & wb) / len(wa | wb) if (wa | wb) else 0\n    return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\n\n\ndef related(story, existing):\n    scored = []\n    for other in existing:\n        if other[\"slug\"] == story[\"slug\"]:\n            continue\n        scored.append({\"slug\": other[\"slug\"], \"score\": similarity(story, other)})\n    scored.sort(key=lambda s: s[\"score\"], reverse=True)\n    return scored[:TOP_N]\n\n\ndef validate(story):\n    for k in (\"slug\", \"title\", \"body\"):\n        if not story.get(k):\n            raise ValueError(f\"missing field: {k}\")\n    if not re.fullmatch(r\"[a-z0-9-]{3,80}\", story[\"slug\"]):\n        raise ValueError(\"bad slug\")\n\n\ndef publish(table, story):\n    \"\"\"Store ``story`` with its related stories. Returns the stored item.\"\"\"\n    validate(story)\n    existing = table.scan(TableName=TABLE_NAME).get(\"Items\", [])\n    item = {\n        \"slug\": story[\"slug\"],\n        \"title\": story[\"title\"],\n        \"tags\": sorted(set(story.get(\"tags\", []))),\n        \"body\": story[\"body\"],\n        \"published_at\": int(time.time()),\n        \"similar\": related(story, existing),\n    }\n    table.put_item(Item=item)\n    log.info(\"publish slug=%s similar=%d stored\", item[\"slug\"], len(item[\"similar\"]))\n    return item\n\n\ndef handler(event, table):\n    \"\"\"Lambda-style entry point for POST /stories. Body is the story as JSON.\"\"\"\n    try:\n        story = json.loads(event.get(\"body\") or \"{}\")\n        stored = publish(table, story)\n        return {\"statusCode\": 201, \"body\": json.dumps({\"slug\": stored[\"slug\"]})}\n    except ValueError as e:\n        return {\"statusCode\": 400, \"body\": json.dumps({\"error\": str(e)})}\n    except Exception:\n        log.exception(\"publish failed\")\n        return {\"statusCode\": 500, \"body\": json.dumps({\"error\": \"Internal Server Error\"})}\n","numLines":79,"startLine":1,"requestedOffset":null,"requestedLimit":2000,"totalLines":null,"wasTruncated":false},"approvalSource":"bypass","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Read","message":"79 lines from src/app.py","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"durationMs":0.0,"decision":"execute","approvalType":"always"}}
{"id":"assistant-faacc1c9-4d31-5004-868b-f82337bd2c4b","sessionId":"cb1b579b-a4ed-295c-9696-f1030ea14b38","turnId":"turn-8bd04679712c34ce8e7fb14ef01d9362","inputEntryId":"user-turn-8bd04679712c34ce8e7fb14ef01d9362-1","createdAt":1794279809813,"updatedAt":1794279809813,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! Now let me create the ANSWER.md file with the cause and fix:"}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
{"id":"effect-39bfac08-1212-5039-9d76-9b415ba6b324","sessionId":"cb1b579b-a4ed-295c-9696-f1030ea14b38","turnId":"turn-8bd04679712c34ce8e7fb14ef01d9362","inputEntryId":"user-turn-8bd04679712c34ce8e7fb14ef01d9362-1","createdAt":1794279809831,"updatedAt":1794279809865,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.write_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.write_file","display":{"summary":"Writing ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(value, 4)`). DynamoDB does not accept float types; it requires numeric values to be `int` or `Decimal`.\n\n- First publish: no existing stories → `similar` list is empty → no score values → succeeds\n- Second publish: one existing story → `similar` list contains `{\"slug\": \"...\", \"score\": 0.9}` where `0.9` is a `float` → DynamoDB rejects with `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` → 500 error\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added import: `from decimal import Decimal`\n2. Changed the return statement in `similarity()` from:\n   ```python\n   return round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)\n   ```\n   to:\n   ```python\n   return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\n   ```\n\nThis ensures the score is stored as a `Decimal` type, which DynamoDB accepts. The `str()` conversion avoids floating-point precision issues when creating the Decimal.\n","suffix":"","verb":"Creating","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Created","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Writing file"},"kind":"file_write","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(value, 4)`). DynamoDB does not accept float types; it requires numeric values to be `int` or `Decimal`.\n\n- First publish: no existing stories → `similar` list is empty → no score values → succeeds\n- Second publish: one existing story → `similar` list contains `{\"slug\": \"...\", \"score\": 0.9}` where `0.9` is a `float` → DynamoDB rejects with `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` → 500 error\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added import: `from decimal import Decimal`\n2. Changed the return statement in `similarity()` from:\n   ```python\n   return round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)\n   ```\n   to:\n   ```python\n   return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\n   ```\n\nThis ensures the score is stored as a `Decimal` type, which DynamoDB accepts. The `str()` conversion avoids floating-point precision issues when creating the Decimal.\n"}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-MZ7H8q/ANSWER.md","content":"## Cause\n\nThe `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` (via `round(value, 4)`). DynamoDB does not accept float types; it requires numeric values to be `int` or `Decimal`.\n\n- First publish: no existing stories → `similar` list is empty → no score values → succeeds\n- Second publish: one existing story → `similar` list contains `{\"slug\": \"...\", \"score\": 0.9}` where `0.9` is a `float` → DynamoDB rejects with `TypeError: Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead.` → 500 error\n\n## Fix\n\nChanged `src/app.py`:\n\n1. Added import: `from decimal import Decimal`\n2. Changed the return statement in `similarity()` from:\n   ```python\n   return round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)\n   ```\n   to:\n   ```python\n   return Decimal(str(round(0.7 * tag_score + 0.3 * word_score, 4)))\n   ```\n\nThis ensures the score is stored as a `Decimal` type, which DynamoDB accepts. The `str()` conversion avoids floating-point precision issues when creating the Decimal.\n","fileExisted":false,"previousContent":null},"approvalSource":"bypass","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Created","message":"ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"durationMs":0.0,"decision":"execute","approvalType":"always"}}
