{"id":"assistant-9367cdfa-2d0b-5077-8d36-7b6aa487d516","sessionId":"cb1b579b-a4ed-295c-9696-f1030ea14b38","turnId":"turn-8bd04679712c34ce8e7fb14ef01d9362","inputEntryId":"user-turn-8bd04679712c34ce8e7fb14ef01d9362-1","createdAt":1794279818827,"updatedAt":1794279818827,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Excellent! Everything works. Let me create a final summary:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Problem identified**: The `similarity()` function in `src/app.py` returns a Python `float` value. DynamoDB doesn't support float types - it only accepts `int` or `Decimal` for numeric values.\n\n**Why it worked once**: The first publish had no existing stories, so the `similar` list was empty (no scores to store). The second publish tried to store similarity scores as floats, causing DynamoDB to reject with a 500 error.\n\n**Fix applied**: \n1. Added `from decimal import Decimal` import\n2. Modified `similarity()` to return `Decimal(str(round(...)))` instead of a float\n\n**Verification**: \n- Multiple publishes now work correctly\n- Existing tests pass\n- The fix prevents the issue from recurring\n\nThe cause and fix are documented in `ANSWER.md`."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
